From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:55:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rest): Rest's regularity is the bedtime regularity the
 Consistency card shows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The regularity in each night's stored Rest (and so its Charge) is now the bedtime
regularity of the «Consistencia» card, from one resolver both read
(VictorSleepNeed.bedtimeRegularity), not the duration variability.

Night D: 1 - SD(bedtime) / 120 min, clamped to 0..1, over the main-night bedtimes of
the last 14 nights within the 28 days up to D (3 at least); WHOOP's imported
sleep_consistency still wins its night. Fixed in that one place, from the card's own
per-session score:
- one bedtime per night, the day's main night (bridged), so naps no longer count as
  bedtimes (a 40-minute nap every third afternoon took a regular sleeper's card to 0);
- a 28-day bound, so a gap in wear never reaches a stale month;
- circular SD, so bedtimes either side of midnight or noon read minutes apart (the old
  fold put an 11:30 day-sleep bedtime on the next day);
- each night on its own clock (DST), with no learned habitual time in the main-night
  pick, so the pass and the screens cannot pick differently;
- the card speaks for the latest night only; no other night's value stands in.

The pass resolves it from the sessions as they will read once it has banked its own
(WhoopRepository.sleepsMergedWith, the same upsert policy) and publishes it; the app
warms it from the store at start. The card, its detail graph, Rest on every screen,
Coupled, the weekly digest and Today's drivers read the published figure; Sleep,
Coupled, Trends and the digest recompose when it changes. Nothing is stored and no
schema changes. The duration regularity stays only in pass 1's unread DayResult.rest
and the Vitality age; the old per-session consistencySeries is no longer read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
